<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhubaneswar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhubaneswar is the capital of the Indian state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>. Near it lie Sisupalgarh, a fortified city of the last centuries BCE often linked with ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinga">Kalinga</a>, and the Jain caves of Udayagiri and Khandagiri. Known as the 'temple city', it has hundreds of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temples, above all the 11th-century Lingaraja temple. It replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuttack">Cuttack</a> as the state capital in 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhubaneswar.jpg" alt="Bhubaneswar" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ashok3932 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bhubaneswar_skyline_121224.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
